# UA lab — webuseragent() verification

Route `ualab:run` (also exposed as a "UA lab" service): opens a webpopup
at `<lab>/start`, lets the lab record the User-Agent CEF actually sent,
then compares it with `popup.webuseragent()`.

Lab server (needs python3):

    python3 -c '
    from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, HTTPServer
    ua = ["?"]
    class H(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
        def do_GET(self):
            if self.path == "/start":
                ua[0] = self.headers.get("User-Agent", "")
                self.send_response(200)
                self.send_header("Content-Type", "text/html")
                self.end_headers()
                self.wfile.write(b"<script>setTimeout(function(){location=\"/done\"},1000)</script>")
            else:
                self.send_response(200); self.end_headers()
                self.wfile.write((ua[0] if self.path == "/ua" else self.headers.get("User-Agent", "")).encode())
    HTTPServer(("127.0.0.1", 18999), H).serve_forever()'

Expected log: `[ua] equal: true` — webuseragent() must return exactly
the UA CEF sends, cf_clearance depends on it.
